speechtext:
Resolved, that the schedule to Bill C-116, an act to amend the Customs Tariff, now before the house, be amended by adding thereto the following:
Tariff item 209e, potassium chloride, British preferential tariff, free, most-favoured-nation tariff, free, general tariff, 25 per cent, (applicable July 3, 1961 to December 31, 1963);
Tariff item 210i, sodium hypochlorite in solution, British preferential tariff, 15 per cent, mostfavoured-nation tariff, 20 per cent, general tariff, 30 per cent, (applicable July 3, 1961 to December 31, 1963);
Tariff item 263e, compounds of tetramethyl lead, in which tetramethyl lead is the preponderant constituent by weight, British preferential tariff, 12| per cent, most-favoured-nation tariff, 12) per cent, general tariff, 25 per cent, (applicable July 3, 1961 to December 31, 1963).

Tariff item 209e, potassium chloride, British preferential tariff, free, most-favoured-nation tariff, free, general tariff, 25 per cent, (applicable July 3, 1961 to December 31, 1963);
Tariff item 210i, sodium hypochlorite in solution, British preferential tariff, 15 per cent, mostfavoured-nation tariff, 20 per cent, general tariff, 30 per cent, (applicable July 3, 1961 to December 31, 1963);
Tariff item 263e, compounds of tetramethyl lead, in which tetramethyl lead is the preponderant constituent by weight, British preferential tariff, 12J per cent, most-favoured-nation tariff, 12', per cent, general tariff, 25 per cent, (applicable July 3, 1961 to December 31, 1963).
